{
  "id": "cloudwatch-asg-live-scaling",
  "name": "CloudWatch → ASG: Live EC2 Scale-Out",
  "category": "Compute & Auto Scaling",
  "difficulty": "Intermediate",
  "description": "Use Send Request through the internal ALB twice at Normal traffic. Each run represents 120 requests over one minute; 60 requests per initial target exceeds the threshold of 50. A new EC2 appears directly on the canvas. Select CloudWatch → Config to change policy type. Watch Launching → InService, cooldown, and the maximum of four instances. Reset scaling removes generated instances. Traffic batches are synthetic teaching inputs, not measured AWS metrics.",
  "learningOutcome": "CloudWatch alarm → simple scaling policy → desired capacity → instance launch/warmup → eligible ALB target. Scaling is real persisted simulator state, not a walkthrough. One subnet; no scale-in or ECS scheduling.",
